(text "Row 2 is the 5V_IN net - the output of U26 (the AP63205 VBAT buck on POWER 1), taken BEFORE U25, the TPS2121\npriority power mux. Servo current therefore never crosses V5_SYS or the mux and is not counted against the\nmux ILM current limit (1.49 A, set by R46); it does count against the buck, which is a 2 A part, so the four\nservo channels share whatever is left of 2 A after the avionics load (~0.3 A typical, 0.6 A peak). Sizing the\n5V_IN copper and budgeting servo current against U26 is an open item in DESIGN_SPEC.\nNothing on this sheet loads V3V3_SYS or USB_VBUS." (at 15 120 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left top)) (uuid 44c3c953-b70a-5957-8cb3-bb7b1b12ce86))
(text "Three stacked Conn_01x04 symbols (J12 signal, J13 5 V, J14 GND) with three 1x04 THT footprints: no 3-row\ngeneric connector symbol or 2.54 mm 3x04 footprint ships with this KiCad install. Place them on 2.54 mm\ncentres at the bottom-left of the board to form a 3x4 servo block in standard servo lead order\n(SIG / 5 V / GND); column n is J12 pin n / J13 pin n / J14 pin n. Through-hole 2.54 mm is deliberate here:\nDESIGN_SPEC \"Physical design\" puts solder pads on every bus and keeps THT pins for leftover IO only." (at 15 155 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left top)) (uuid a5424632-7b2f-5181-9f50-f8f6532ad2eb))
(text "PWM MAP (this sheet)\nPWM5 = GPIO10\nPWM6 = GPIO11\nPWM7 = GPIO14\nPWM8 = GPIO15\n\nON THE ESC PAD ROW (J3, POWER 1)\nPWM1 = GPIO2\nPWM2 = GPIO3\nPWM3 = GPIO4\nPWM4 = GPIO5" (at 15 195 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left top)) (uuid fbccdc73-f196-58d6-9a90-da558b83cb5b))
(embedded_fonts no))
